Rule 3 (shape alignment for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0))
>>
Rule 4 (first dimension of a tensor matches second dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 1)
